# Next-gen store identity stays isolated

Alpha and beta builds of this app are a separate store app from the old-gen production app.
`apps/mobile/app.config.ts` is the identity: iOS `bundleIdentifier` and Android `package` are
`com.podverse.app.next`. The display name is Podverse Next.

## Until the operator explicitly says to replace the old production app

- Do not change `bundleIdentifier` or `package` away from `com.podverse.app.next`.
- Do not set `ascAppId` in `apps/mobile/eas.json` to the old Podverse App Store app. It must be a
  new App Store Connect app whose bundle id is `com.podverse.app.next`.
- Do not upload a binary to the old Play listing or reuse that app's signing key. Play matches the
  package name, so `com.podverse.app.next` is a different app.
- `PROFILE=production` still means the next-gen listing. It does not mean the old production app.
- EAS credentials (certificates, profiles, Play service account, App Store Connect API key) stay
  the next-gen set, stored on EAS, not in git.

A binary whose id is `com.podverse.app.next` cannot update the old app. The way that app gets
replaced is a later, explicit change of this identity onto the old listing, with the old signing
key. Do not do that as part of an alpha or beta build.

The later cutover checklist (same bundle id, same listing, in-place upgrade) is
**mobile-deep-links-and-prod-cutover**. The old production bundle id is not assumed here.
